One mole of an ideal monoatomic gas is first heated isobarically. In this 
process, it does 20 J of work. Then, it is heated isothermally, receiving the 
same amount of heat as in the first case. How much work (in joules) does the gas
do in the second case? Wrap your entire response with double quotation marks. 
Answer with at least 2 letters. Your answer must contain exactly 10 bullet 
